"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "C and JPM provide nearly identical definitions of VIE criteria. C defines a VIE if (i) equity is insufficient to finance activities without subordinated support, or (ii) equity investors cannot make significant decisions or absorb proportionate losses/returns. JPM defines VIEs as entities that 'either (1) lack sufficient equity to permit the entity to finance its activities without additional subordinated financial support from other parties, or (2) have equity investors that do not have the ability to make significant decisions... or do not have the obligation to absorb the expected losses, or do not have the right to receive the residual returns.' The language and specific criteria for identifying a VIE are substantively the same.",
